<title>USA: Univision Communications Q4 shr up.</title>
<headline>Univision Communications Q4 shr up.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Univision Communications Inc.</p>
<p>On a pro forma basis, the Company's three and twelve months</p>
<p>				results were as follows:</p>
<p>			Three Months Ended	Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>    $, Millions	   December 31,		 December 31,</p>
<p>(Except Per Share)     1996  1995  Change  1996  1995  Change</p>
<p> Net Revenues	     106.5  89.3    19%  370.3  321.3  15%</p>
<p> Broadcast Cash Flow     45.4  32.2    41%  149.7  121.3  23%</p>
<p> EBITDA			42.8  29.1    47%  140.1  111.6  26%</p>
<p> Extraordinary Loss	  --    --     --  (11.2) (16.3)  --</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)	 19.3   5.8   231%   25.1  (5.9)   --</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss)</p>
<p>  Per Common Share (A)   0.33  0.10   231%   0.44  (0.10)  --</p>
<p>Weighted Average Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding		57.7  57.7     --   57.7   57.7   --</p>
<p>NOTE: (A) Excluding the extraordinary losses for the twelve months ended December 31, 1995 and 1996, which related to the pro forma repurchase and defeasance of the outstanding 11.75% Senior Subordinated Notes at January 1, 1995 and 1996, the earnings per share for the twelve months in 1996 were $.63 compared to $.18 in the 1995 period.</p>
